k when relevant\n- [ ] In a managed Story worktree the candidate is left UNCOMMITTED in the worktree for the handoff to snapshot — never commit on the Story branch. A producer commit moves the branch tip off the recorded checkpoint and the handoff refuses with change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint; repair with `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\n- [ ] Implementation matches AC\n- [ ] Solution fits project architecture\n- [ ] Tests green\n- [ ] Gate, refusal, validation, authorization, and attestation behavior attacked, not read — positive-path-only evidence is not accepted\n- [ ] If review does not accept the work — verdict evidence added and status routed by the explicit verdict branches\n\n## Task\n\n- **ID:** TASK-260830-2x16gz\n- **Title:** TASK-260830-2x16gz: test-peer-auth-and-hostile-network-failures\n- **Parent:** STORY-260830-1kiyj6\n\n### Description\n\nProve unknown peers, key changes, spoofed host IDs, disconnects, replay, oversized frames, and disclosure mismatches fail closed. This is an implementation deliverable, not a specification rewrite.\n\n### Scope\n\nAdopted current authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0, commit 0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6. Primary implementation-conformance owner for section 11.10.4 / AC-HOST-001, across both OpenSSH and native Tailscale SSH, with real certificate chains, handshake, timeout/race, custody, revocation and generation tests. Use section 11.10.5 and its upstream publication vectors as source evidence only; do not claim their synthetic passes establish executed product support. Historical scope retained without weakening: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.5.0 (commit 28bf96d7dd7ebf3cd9e2ccd91d35b8660699dd5c); \\u00a76, \\u00a711.1, \\u00a716.1. Work only inside the peer-configuration-and-authentication story boundary. Activation waits for signed STORY-260908-18woqo landing; this binding does not accept or alter the preserved partial implementation.\n\n### Acceptance Criteria\n\nProduction behavior demonstrates: Prove unknown peers, key changes, spoofed host IDs, disconnects, replay, oversized frames, and disclosure mismatches fail closed. Exact contract fixtures and negative/refusal cases pass; crash/idempotency evidence is included when the operation mutates durable state; no unsupported capability is advertised.\n\n## Instructions\n\n### TASK-260830-2x16gz_ordering-decision.md\n> Primary dependency repair preserving the full seven-case conformance scope and existing RPC implementation owner\n\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-2x16gz/TASK-260830-2x16gz_ordering-decision.md`\n\n- Byte count: `3371`\n- Content digest: `sha256:62474f66670c8c7bed74d140a6758ba3dda82471c73e4c9331e7aac5c0025ebc`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-2x16gz_producer.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-2x16gz/TASK-260830-2x16gz_producer.md`\n\n- Byte count: `7630`\n- Content digest: `sha256:4323e36821d9715ff460f7ecd9679e461182aa4582345dfe8abc02e4eb8eaac1`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-2x16gz_republish-rev1.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-2x16gz/TASK-260830-2x16gz_republish-rev1.md`\n\n- Byte count: `4794`\n- Content digest: `sha256:3c801e2be205e6f27a1d634537a861bfb3d422cb12681605d3c157ac28f7e33a`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n### TASK-260830-2x16gz_reviewer-cr1.md\nAttached file: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/resources/TASK-260830-2x16gz/TASK-260830-2x16gz_reviewer-cr1.md`\n\n- Byte count: `7232`\n- Content digest: `sha256:2915dd128b91e3e1238012537300642d7bef99bc792e174018cc1228c8c41736`\n- Access: read-only\n\n\n\n\n\n## Evidence and Safety\n\n- Add/update a task-scoped outcome named `TASK-260830-2x16gz_*` before handoff:\n  `task-board m 'add_resource(TASK-260830-2x16gz, name=TASK-260830-2x16gz_results.md, content=\"...\", type=outcome, description=\"Handoff evidence\")'`\n- Gating, refusing, validating, authorizing, or attesting behavior ships with negative tests that fail when the gate admits what it must reject; prove the bound by narrowing it, not only by deleting it, and name the production call site. Shapes and incidents: `references/negative-evidence.md`.\n- An absence and a failure to read are different facts; report unknown instead of inferring a property from a proxy signal.\n- Stop-The-Line only for an evidence-backed external blocker or unresolved human-only product/platform/architecture/approval decision. Persist evidence, failed attempts, options/tradeoffs, recommendation, and exact input needed; otherwise rework autonomously.\n- You are licensed to attempt to DEFEAT any gate, refusal, validation, authorization, or attestation under review, and to reject a change whose only evidence is positive-path. Grep for callers before believing a guard is in force; a delete-only mutant proves existence, not coverage.\n- Review read-only and record exactly one evidence-backed verdict: accepted → `done`; changes requested → `to-dev` or `analysis`; genuine Stop-The-Line → `blocked`. Never leave the task in `reviewing`.\n- With a `Change Request Under Review` section, accept via `task-board m 'accept_cr(ID, revision=N, evidence=ID_review-verdict.md)'`. It writes `accepted` and `integrating` atomically and routes the element to `integrating` — accepted work never stays in `reviewing` and never reaches `done` from here. The accepted revision is bound to its producer role and archetype; only a new tracked run with that exact producer role and archetype may checkpoint or integrate it, and the orchestrator routes that run but does not close the leaf. `accept_cr` takes no acknowledgement argument, and only the reviewer run that was handed the revision may call it.\n- Reviewer-archetype runs must not supply `commit_ack` and must not escalate the commit-or-acknowledge decision to the human; record acceptance evidence and leave every `done` transition to the producer side.\n\n## Working Directory\nBoard directory: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board`\n\nWork in the project root. Never edit board files directly.\n\n## Story Workspace\n\nYou are running in an isolated Git worktree for STORY-260830-1kiyj6.\n\n- Workspace path: `.temp/STORY-260830-1kiyj6/worktree` (this is your working directory)\n- Branch: `task-board/story/STORY-260830-1kiyj6`, forked from `main`\n- Authoritative board: `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.task-board` (already exported as `TASK_BOARD_DIR`)\n\nMake every repository change here. Do not commit, switch, rebase, merge, or delete this branch, and do not run `task-board` against the `.task-board` copy inside this worktree — it is a checkout artifact, not the board. Integration into trunk is the orchestrator's step, not yours.\n\nLeave your work UNCOMMITTED in the worktree — the handoff snapshots the working tree against the recorded checkpoint. A commit of your own on this branch is refused at handoff with `change_request_candidate_committed_past_checkpoint`, and the repair is `git reset --soft <checkpoint_oid>` before completing again.\n\n## Change Request Under Review\n\n- Change Request: `CR-TASK-260830-2x16gz-1` revision `1` (state `ready`)\n- Element: `TASK-260830-2x16gz`, integration scope: `STORY-260830-1kiyj6`\n- Branch: `task-board/story/STORY-260830-1kiyj6`\n- Base OID: `e4e3e8834675cf3814effd3b2673b4931dfbf311`\n- Candidate tree OID: `1d03fbc7fe3ecd73347eb424bc5de1ce94df7370`\n- Repository delta: `present`\n- Patch resource: `TASK-260830-2x16gz_change-request_rev1.patch` (sha256 `4384b5ac4381f9c9d697808cee9c00394e1bc05c51aeaec0d4c00d86ccd41b23`)\n\n```bash\ngit -C . diff e4e3e8834675cf3814effd3b2673b4931dfbf311 1d03fbc7fe3ecd73347eb424bc5de1ce94df7370          # the exact reviewable delta\ngit -C . diff --stat e4e3e8834675cf3814e