ng different identity facts in hello and certificate; contracts.rpc other than [\"5.0.0\"]; Structured Error version drift), timeout/race (silent peer past the handshake and hello deadlines; a peer stalling mid-request against the configured RPC timeout; two concurrent connections from one peer), custody (leaf private key read from a wrong-permission file or a foreign store refused by the ResolvedPaths pair; a copied key authenticates until revoked — assert both halves as the pinned text states), revocation and generation (revoke a live peer: idle and in-flight streams close within one second per the pinned text — measure it; rotation admits the new tuple only after explicit enrollment, retire_at bounds, no second rotation before revocation; a stale generation at dispatch and at a mutation boundary refused under concurrent mutation), migration/downgrade refusals (Config-4 selecting a legacy route, an RPC-4 hello on the host channel, a plaintext preface), both role failures (initiator refuses a bad server; responder refuses a bad client), stale/failed reads (an unreadable trust store or marker is an integrity failure, not \"absent\"), recovery bypasses (a retry that changes the operation ID or body is refused; no new-session/fresh-handle substitution); (3) every vector asserts the exact Section 15 class and exit and that nothing durable changed (census the state dir before/after); (4) the Section 11.10.5 upstream policy vectors are source evidence only — do not implement a policy reader and do not claim their synthetic passes as executed support; (5) narrowing mutants for every new assertion family with a shipped harness (per-plant raw logs, subprocess exits, an applied harmless SURVIVED control), plus the seven original conformance cases of this task re-derived with n-of-m through the authenticated channel; (6) a conformance matrix mapping every AC-HOST-001 clause, HC-* gate and hostile-network row to a test, a not-executed stated bound (native Tailscale SSH; platform lanes other than this host) or NOT APPLICABLE with owner. This is the FINAL leaf (story_final CR): carry the Story-close items — internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json bindings for 6.6/11.10/11.10.1-11.10.5/16.1 and the acceptance case AC-HOST-001 bound to the real conformance suite with honest coverage text (executed lanes versus stated bounds), reviewedOwnershipCanonicalSHA256 re-pinned (precedent Stories 3drr2m/3jqsx1/3m2mw8/2jylym); README sections for internal/hostchannel/rpcwire (if missing) and your suite with test commands and no capability claim (no ax command exists); LOGBOOK entry; the candidate's task-board.config.json must remain byte-identical to trunk except the rpcwire fuzz gate already added by z1yxg9 (if you add a conformance command, say so explicitly and keep it bounded). Managed Story worktree contract: .temp/STORY-260830-1kiyj6/worktree on branch task-board/story/STORY-260830-1kiyj6 whose tip is the z1yxg9 checkpoint; the preserved packet directories under .temp are read-only; leave the candidate UNCOMMITTED, never commit on the Story branch, never edit .task-board directly, never self-accept; origin/main has moved to e4e3e88 (release-agnostic validation command 21) — run task-board worktree refresh-candidate TASK-260830-2x16gz first and restore any trunk-changed path the refresh left stale with a single-path git checkout HEAD -- <path>; before handoff verify git status shows only candidate paths (no __pycache__, no .pyc; PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1). Evidence contract as in the repository DoD. Read the Curator-managed go-testing-tools skill first; all CI local; run the full configured validation suite once before the handoff; hand off no later than 3.5 hours in (an 8-point leaf: if the full matrix cannot be finished, hand off a reviewable slice with the remaining rows enumerated precisely — the Story-close items are mandatory). Attach TASK-260830-2x16gz_results.md, TASK-260830-2x16gz_conformance-matrix.md and TASK-260830-2x16gz_producer-evidence.tar.gz (a real gzip archive), keep the checklist current, then task-board handoff TASK-260830-2x16gz --role developer and exit promptly. Canonical CLI /Users/iv/.curator/global/bin/task-board. Model: muse-spark max. The independent reviewer will be muse-spark xhigh while codex is out of quota.","correlation_facts":{"tool_name":"read_file","outcome":"success"}}}
