2657:11.10.2 store; neither a certificate nor private-key bytes belong in TOML.\\n7110:11.10 instead and MUST NOT enter this legacy path.\\n8007:### 11.10 Host Channel 1.0.0 and Mesh RPC 5.0.0\\n8014:#### 11.10.1 Launch, TLS and dispatch\\n8036:full certificate authentication on every connection, and the Section 11.10.2\\n8098:#### 11.10.2 Certificate issuance and enrolled trust\\n8189:#### 11.10.3 Rotation, revocation and authorization generations\\n8245:#### 11.10.4 Assurance and executable fixture bounds\\n8276:#### 11.10.5 Executable admission obligations\\n8298:Section 6.6 and 11.10.1–4 explanations are checked against the review-bound\\n11159:Configuration 4.0.0 (Sections 6.6 and 11.10). The flag is accepted only on\\n14971:For Config-4/RPC-5, Sections 6.6 and 11.10 additionally require enrolled\\n14982:| AX host authentication | Host keys, credential/trust stores and backups, enrollment authority, TLS secrets and generation caches (Section 11.10) |\\n15139:Section 6.6 and Section 11.10 define the new containing contracts and explicit\\n15889:validator against the exact ten Section 11.10.4 gate families, executable\\n15890:Section 11.10.5 policy and <code>fixtures/host_channel_conformance.json</code>.\\n15914:| Mutual host authentication and credential lifecycle | Sections 1.5, 6.6, 11.10, 16, 17.1; AC-HOST-001 and SPEC-PUB-HOST-001 |\\n16160:Section 11.10 design, not a claim that those sources implement AX. The\\n16203:| Host Channel / Host Trust Store | Sections 6.6 and 11.10; host_channel_conformance.json | Missing/forged credential, wrong role/UUID/hello, duplicate mapping, stale generation, idle revocation, rollback, legacy fallback, replicated keys; cover all ten gate families and Section 11.10.5 field obligations with token-preserving scope changes and regenerated-table behavior tests |\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 2726,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 682,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
