{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8b9","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aece-231f-7991-85b6-ba6bca7c9720"},"sequence":695,"recorded_at":1780531400001385,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e70d9852-000b-4121-b33e-b53bebd87eae","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e70d9852-000b-4121-b33e-b53bebd87eae","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e70d9852-000b-4121-b33e-b53bebd87eae"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aecf-775c-7700-9e7b-5a847ba9a0e4"},"task_id":"01a0aecf-775c-7700-9e7b-5a847ba9a0e4","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aecf-775c-7700-9e7b-5a847ba9a0e4","chunk":"Read text file `/tmp/rev-2x16gz/z1yxg9-verdict.md`.\n1|# Review verdict — CR-TASK-260830-z1yxg9-1 revision 1 (ACCEPT)\n2|\n3|Reviewer run: RUN-260917-00d532 (reviewer). Candidate tree\n4|9d0c99b0669444ae77677348f54f1b4b1d791881 over base\n5|ae5a4cc5394ef80fc2fc3ef12965acc0670cb5a4 — 30 paths, no board files.\n6|Normative authority: spec v0.6.0 §§11.10/11.10.1–11.10.5, 11.9,\n7|11.2/11.3, 15.1/15.3. Credential owner hosttrust accepted under\n8|CR-TASK-260909-2ez769-12 (not re-litigated; candidate consumes it).\n9|\n10|Method: isolated immutable probes only. Candidate bytes materialized with\n11|`git archive <candidate-oid>` to /private/tmp scratch; mutation probes via\n12|`go -overlay` or scratch-copy edits; the live Story worktree, index,\n13|branch and HEAD were never mutated; no product edits, commits,\n14|checkpoints, or integration. PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 for every harness.\n15|\n16|## Verdict: ACCEPT (no P1; two P3 hardening notes in §8)\n17|\n18|## 1. Restoration — verified, faithful\n19|\n20|- Packet manifest: all 15 packet bytes match manifest sha256 (recomputed).\n21|- Candidate fixtures contracts-v3/v4 and hello-request/response-v2 match\n22|  manifest digests byte-for-byte.\n23|- rpcwire code/README extended for RPC 5.0.0; mutations.py extended by the\n24|  declared v5-exact probe; contracts-v5.json added and differs from v4 by\n25|  exactly the `\"rpc\": [\"5.0.0\"]` line.\n26|- UNRESOLVED_QUESTIONS.md dropped: faithful — it recorded the inbound\n27|  identity association as open and v0.6.0 §11.10 resolves it (mutual TLS\n28|  1.3 over verified enrolled certificates before hello/dispatch); the\n29|  resolution is recorded in both READMEs, LOGBOOK and results.\n30|- Tracked deltas: README section appended (15.1 5/7, 15.3 2/3 unchanged,\n31|  no new discharge claimed); ownership gaps rewritten with coverage\n32|  levels and clause enumerations unchanged; traceability digest\n33|  5102d3bc… (tracecheck green); task-board.config.json adds exactly one\n34|  fuzz-gate line, no other field touched.\n35|\n36|## 2. AC accounting — 7 of 7 rows driven through production entries\n37|\n38|All named tests exist in the candidate and pass (full suite green):\n39|\n40|| # | Row | Production call sites | Named tests (confirmed present+green) |\n41|| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n42|| 1 | Request/response correlation | Dial + Call + Serve | TestFullHandshakeHelloAndOperation, TestHelloResponseCorrelation |\n43|| 2 | Hello maps and nonce echo | Serve/Dial hello exchange | TestFullHandshakeHelloAndOperation, TestRefusesInvalidHello/* |\n44|| 3 | Namespace/cardinality | Call(\"inventory.roots\") dispatch | TestInventoryRootsThroughChannel |\n45|| 4 | Offered limits | hello validation both roles | TestFullHandshakeHelloAndOperation, TestOversizeHelloLine |\n46|| 5 | Structured Error framing | Serve refusal frames, Dial mapping | TestRefusesNonHelloBeforeHello, TestHelloFailureMapping/* |\n47|| 6 | Bilateral admission | AuthorizeDispatch at hello both roles | TestRefusesHelloUUIDMismatch, TestRefusesServerHelloUUIDMismatch, TestRefusesNotAllowlisted, TestRefusesDestinationMismatch |\n48|| 7 | Deadlines/generation | bounded I/O, stale gates, WatchGeneration | TestHelloDeadline/*, TestHelloWriteDeadline, TestDispatchTimeout, TestStaleGenerationAtDispatch/*, TestStaleGenerationAtMutation, TestDispatchExpiryClosesWithoutFrame, TestWatchGeneration |\n49|\n50|Crash/idempotency: the channel writes no durable state — proven by static\n51|census (TestStaticWriteCensus) + runtime census (TestRuntimeWriteCensus:\n52|state trees, trust bytes, temp tripwire); trust commits stay atomic in\n53|hosttrust. No crash-recovery behavior attested, correctly so. No\n54|unsupported capability advertised: docs state no `ax` command, no SSH\n55|process launch, no listener, no provider plugin, no object exchange;\n56|launch selection is a computed Config-4 argv only.\n57|\n58|## 3. Conformance (code read in full: channel/server/client/launch)\n59|\n60|TLS 1.3 only (shared Min=Max builder), NextProtos exactly [ax-host/1],\n61|no tickets, nil client cache, enrolled-roots-only pools (no system pool\n62|in non-test code), VerifyConnection supplementing (never replacing)\n63|standard verification, UUID-SAN ServerName, 65 535-byte authority bound,\n64|10 s handshake/hello deadlines enforced by stream close, 1 MiB handshake\n65|cap, 8 MiB line / 5 MiB object limits, no app bytes before handshake,\n66|hello success validated before any other op, current-generation dispatch\n67|and WithMutationAuthorization boundaries, exporter/key-log material never\n68|persisted. Refusal semantics exact: ≤1 encrypted Error 1.3.0 then close\n69|for pre-hello violations (host_identity_mismatch/peer_not_allowlisted\n70|exit 7, incompatible_protocol exit 6 only when known), silent close for\n71|unframeable/foreign-major input, TLS-alert-only pre-handshake,\n72|authentication_failed 7 / transport_failure 8 / invalid_config 3 on the\n73|initiator. axerror diff adds only the {rpc,5}→1.3.0 row (unbound probe\n74|5→6); no new enum or exit code. HC-MIGRATE takes Host Channel 1 + RPC 5\n75|only from Config-4 and refuses legacy; §11.10.5 correctly not\n76|implemented as a runtime policy reader. HC-PARITY is a stated bound\n77|(abstract Stream, no SSH branch — confirmed by grep); same-profile tests\n78|run over the agnostic Stream.\n79|\n80|## 4. Independent mutant evidence (all rerun by reviewer, per-plant logs\n81|in the evidence tarball)\n82|\n83|- rpcwire harness (isolated copy): 1 neutral passed + 34 narrowing KILLED,\n84|  incl. v5-exact and the token-preserving common-data-model probe (killed\n85|  behaviorally by TestFrameRefusals/duplicate).\n86|- hostchannel harness (isolated copy): 1 neutral passed + 22 narrowing\n87|  KILLED + census-evasion KILLED behaviorally by TestRuntimeWriteCensus\n88|  (passes the static census by design) + 1 documented SURVIVED\n89|  (client-cache, see §5).\n90|- Reviewer-owned narrowing mutants on arms the producer did not mutate\n91|  (scratch copy, restored to pristine after each; raw logs attached):\n92|  M1 ALPN admits exactly \"ax-host/2\" — KILLED by new scratch vector\n93|  TestOwnRefusesAxHost2ALPN while TestVerifyPeerRefusals/alpn stays\n94|  green on the mutant (proves narrowing; the existing suite alone would\n95|  not catch this weakening); M2 client generation admits exactly +1 —\n96|  KILLED by client_refuses_to_send; M3 ServerName skips UUID parse —\n97|  KILLED by bad_destination; M4 helloRefusal maps mismatch→protocol —\n98|  KILLED by host_identity_mismatch mapping test; harmless comment-only\n99|  control passes (SURVIVED as expected).\n100|- KILLED stability: hostchannel suite green 3× (initial, -race, stability\n101|  rerun: 98 subtests pass), rpcwire green 4×+, full repo suite\n102|  `go test ./... -count=1`: 31 packages ok, exit 0.\n103|\n104|## 5. The client-cache SURVIVED — accepted as harmless, correctly bounded\n105|\n106|A caching client cannot resume against a server that issues no tickets,\n107|so no behavioral test through the public API can distinguish the mutant:\n108|there is no cache-injection hook and nothing is ever stored. The\n109|complementary arm (server issues tickets) IS killed by\n110|TestRefusesResumption via the `tickets` probe. One-sided weakening with\n111|the pair covered — accept.\n112|\n113|## 6. Gates run green here\n114|\n115|`go test ./internal/rpcwire ./internal/hostchannel -race -count=1`: ok.\n116|FuzzUntrustedEnvelopes 200x: PASS (200 execs). Coverage reproduced\n117|exactly: hostchannel 81.6%, rpcwire 97.8%. `go vet`: clean. `gofmt -l`:\n118|empty. `go build ./...`: clean (via full test compile). tracecheck:\n119|exit 0. cataloggen -check: exit 0. Candidate tree carries zero\n120|__pycache__/.pyc entries.\n121|\n122|## 7. Reran-vs-accepted\n123|\n124|Reran myself: everything in §§1–6 (restoration sha, fixture diffs,\n125|config/axerror diffs, both harnesses in full, 4 own mutants + control,\n126|full suite, race, fuzz 200x, cover, vet/gofmt, tracecheck, cataloggen,\n127|forbidden-pattern greps, 27/27 named-test existence). Accepted from\n128|attached evidence (spot-checked, not re-executed byte-for-byte):\n129|producer per-probe raw logs (format confirmed present in evidence zip,\n130|70 files) and the validation log's board-health tail (pre-existing\n131|MISSING_ACTIVITY noise, exit 0 — not candidate-related).\n132|\n133|## 8. P3 hardening notes (non-blocking)\n134|\n135|- P3: add an \"ax-host/2\" same-family ALPN case to\n136|  TestVerifyPeerRefusals — M1 proved the committed suite only refuses the\n137|  unrelated \"rogue-alpn\" token while the supplement enforces exact\n138|  equality. (Reviewer scratch vector TestOwnRefusesAxHost2ALPN\n139|  demonstrates the test; not added to the candidate — reviewer makes no\n140|  product edits.)\n141|- P3: TestInvalidActivation/bad_destination takes ~10 s (real handshake\n142|  deadline) — consider a shortened deadline hook for that vector, as\n143|  already done elsewhere.\n144|\n145|## 9. Handoff state\n146|\n147|Candidate left UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no commit, checkpoint,\n148|integration, or landing performed by this run. Live `git status` shows\n149|only the candidate paths plus pre-existing worktree `.task-board`\n150|checkout noise (diagnosed: the 34 board paths are absent from the\n151|candidate tree itself — verified via `git diff base candidate --stat`:\n152|exactly the 30 declared files).","final_result":true}}}
