{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000c8e3","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aece-231f-7991-85b6-ba6bca7c9720"},"sequence":716,"recorded_at":1780531400001427,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e70d9852-000b-4121-b33e-b53bebd87eae","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e70d9852-000b-4121-b33e-b53bebd87eae","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e70d9852-000b-4121-b33e-b53bebd87eae"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aecf-a7f7-7352-9793-9fb56bead62f"},"task_id":"01a0aecf-a7f7-7352-9793-9fb56bead62f","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aecf-a7f7-7352-9793-9fb56bead62f","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-16-1\",\n  \"command\": \"grep -n \\\"11.10.3\\\\|AC-HOST-001\\\\|11.10.1\\\" internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json | head -n 40\\necho \\\"===\\\"\\npython3 -c \\\"import json; d=json.load(open('internal/traceability/ownership.v0.6.0.json')); print(type(d)); ks=list(d.keys())[:20] if isinstance(d,dict) else len(d); print(ks)\\\" 2>&1 | head -n 20\",\n  \"description\": \"Check ownership bindings for revocation\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"2846:      \\\"id\\\": \\\"AC-HOST-001\\\",\\n4189:        \\\"AC-HOST-001\\\"\\n4192:      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Migrate admits explicit migration targets; TASK-260909-2ez769 implemented the Section 6.6 Config-4 host-channel migration with enrolled credentials, atomic replacement and dual-invocation refusal, and the AC-HOST-001 suite proves a v4 document without the required closed mesh.host_channel table refuses at load with no legacy fallback (TestHostileV4WithoutHostChannelBinding). No clause of 6.6 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about its obligations. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260909-2ez769.\\\"\\n4207:      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"ForRelease projects the Section 11.10 RPC-5 operation vocabulary only. TASK-260830-z1yxg9 implements Host Channel 1.0.0 over RPC 5.0.0 in internal/hostchannel: mutual TLS 1.3 with the exact ax-host/1 ALPN over an abstract ordered binary Stream, enrolled-certificate identity via hosttrust snapshots, authorized hello on both roles, current-generation dispatch and mutation boundaries, and the specified Error 1.3.0 refusal framing. The ten HC-* gates of 11.10.4 run as executable positive/negative fixture families (gates_test.go registry). No clause of 11.10 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim about its obligations. Section 11.10.5 is an upstream synthetic source validator, not an AX runtime reader, and is not implemented here. There is no ax CLI, SSH process launch, or provider plugin. TASK-260830-2x16gz executes the AC-HOST-001 hostile-network conformance suite over the landed entries, including the real OpenSSH loopback carrier lane, with native Tailscale SSH and non-host lanes as stated bounds. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-z1yxg9.\\\"\\n4212:        \\\"section:11.10.1\\\"\\n4219:        \\\"AC-HOST-001\\\"\\n4222:      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 11.10.1 launch, TLS and dispatch runs in internal/hostchannel: Serve completes mutual TLS 1.3 with the exact ax-host/1 ALPN over an ordered binary Stream, enforces the handshake and hello deadlines with the 1 MiB handshake cap, and refuses pre-authentication application bytes; the AC-HOST-001 suite drives the real OpenSSH loopback carrier (exact ServeArgv on the wire, TLS records first, no PTY, bounded stderr) and the hostile matrix through Dial/Serve/Call. Native Tailscale SSH is a stated bound, never executed. No clause of 11.10.1 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-2x16gz.\\\"\\n4234:        \\\"AC-HOST-001\\\"\\n4237:      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 11.10.2 issuance and enrolled trust runs in internal/hosttrust: IssueCredential mints P-256 root/leaf pairs with destroyed root keys, VerifyProfile checks the Host Credential Profile 1 fields at enrollment and handshake, and Enroll commits exact leaf/root/SPKI tuples; the AC-HOST-001 suite drives unknown-peer, key-change and custody vectors through the real entries. No clause of 11.10.2 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-2x16gz.\\\"\\n4242:        \\\"section:11.10.3\\\"\\n4249:        \\\"AC-HOST-001\\\"\\n4252:      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 11.10.3 rotation, revocation and authorization generations runs in internal/hosttrust: Rotate admits fresh-key tuples with a bounded retire_at, Revoke commits revocation with generation+1, and dispatch and mutation boundaries fence stale generations; the AC-HOST-001 suite measures revoke-to-fence latency under one second for dispatched work and proves refused retries never rebind. Measured bound: an idle stream with zero traffic does not self-close within one second (no background watchdog in serveLoop); the next dispatch fences and WatchGeneration reports the commit. No clause of 11.10.3 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-2x16gz.\\\"\\n4264:        \\\"AC-HOST-001\\\"\\n4267:      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 11.10.4 assurance runs as the ten HC-* gate families over internal/hostchannel: VerifyPeer supplements standard TLS verification with exact enrolled leaf/root/key matching, current profile validity and trust state, and the AC-HOST-001 suite executes every hostile-network row (unknown peers, key changes, spoofed host IDs, disconnects, replay, oversized frames, disclosure mismatches) through Dial/Serve/Call with per-vector refusal classes and state censuses. Native Tailscale SSH and non-host platform lanes are stated bounds. No clause of 11.10.4 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim. Pending implementation owner: TASK-260830-2x16gz.\\\"\\n4279:        \\\"AC-HOST-001\\\"\\n4282:      \\\"gap\\\": \\\"Section 16.1 trusted mesh model is enforced at the authorization boundary in internal/hosttrust: AuthorizeDispatch admits only explicitly allowlisted UUIDs with exact enrolled leaf/root/SPKI matches and current trust state, and refuses discovered-but-unenrolled peers, spoofed hello identities and stale generations; the AC-HOST-001 suite drives those vectors through the real channel entries. No clause of 16.1 is enumerated against an acceptance case, so the registry makes no clause-level claim.\\\"\\n4314:      \\\"evidence\\\": \\\"The pinned section explicitly calls the predicates synthetic execution context and separates detailed DER, custody and runtime boundaries from policy witnesses. No policy-reader declaration exists in the tree; production host-channel admission is proven by the AC-HOST-001 suite over the real Dial/Serve/Call entries instead.\\\"\\n===\\n<class 'dict'>\\n['format', 'format_version', 'source', 'acceptance_cases', 'ownership', 'unowned_sections']\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5675,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1419,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
