{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d0eb","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aece-231f-7991-85b6-ba6bca7c9720"},"sequence":1744,"recorded_at":1780531400003483,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e70d9852-000b-4121-b33e-b53bebd87eae","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e70d9852-000b-4121-b33e-b53bebd87eae","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e70d9852-000b-4121-b33e-b53bebd87eae"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aee5-137e-7633-a316-a9d7e8515340"},"task_id":"01a0aee5-137e-7633-a316-a9d7e8515340","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aee5-137e-7633-a316-a9d7e8515340","chunk":"{\n  \"chunk_id\": \"exec-48-1\",\n  \"command\": \"echo \\\"=== stray artifacts ===\\\"\\ngit status --porcelain 2>&1 | grep -i \\\"pycache\\\\|\\\\.pyc\\\\|sshd\\\\|hc-evict\\\\|mutant\\\\|plant\\\" || echo \\\"no-stray-plants\\\"\\nfind internal/hostchannel internal/traceability -name \\\"__pycache__\\\" -o -name \\\"*.pyc\\\" 2>&1 | head -n 5; echo \\\"pycache-scan-done\\\"\\nls /tmp/hc-evict 2>&1 || echo \\\"no-hc-evict-leak\\\"\\necho \\\"=== README capability claims ===\\\"\\ngrep -n -i \\\"ax command\\\\|ax rpc\\\\|native tailscale.*support\\\\|tailscale.*pass\\\" README.md internal/hostchannel/README.md 2>&1 | head -n 20\\necho \\\"=== README test commands ===\\\"\\ngrep -n \\\"go test\\\" internal/hostchannel/README.md 2>&1 | head -n 10\\necho \\\"=== LOGBOOK newest-first ===\\\"\\nhead -n 25 LOGBOOK.md 2>&1\",\n  \"description\": \"Check hygiene and doc claims\",\n  \"exit_code\": 0,\n  \"terminal_status\": \"completed\",\n  \"output\": \"=== stray artifacts ===\\nno-stray-plants\\npycache-scan-done\\nls: /tmp/hc-evict: No such file or directory\\nno-hc-evict-leak\\n=== README capability claims ===\\nREADME.md:2990:`ax rpc serve --stdio`, including the canonical endpoint grammar's port and IPv6\\nREADME.md:3025:for the fixed `ax rpc serve --stdio` command. Policy arguments precede peer\\ninternal/hostchannel/README.md:50:  (`ax rpc serve --stdio --host-channel 1.0.0`) under Configuration 4.\\n=== README test commands ===\\n77:`go test ./internal/hostchannel -count=1` (race-clean): full\\n=== LOGBOOK newest-first ===\\n# Flight Logbook\\n\\n> Institutional memory. Concise, factual, high-signal.\\n> Newest entries first. One block per insight.\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260830-2x16gz — hostile-network conformance suite + AC-HOST-001 (final leaf)\\n- DELIVERED: `internal/hostchannel/hostile_test.go` + `hostile_carrier_test.go` re-derive all seven story cases through the real `Dial`/`Serve`/`Call` entries with per-vector Section 15 classes and state censuses, and execute the AC-HOST-001 rows: real OpenSSH loopback carrier (unprivileged `sshd`, forced command, exact `ServeArgv` on the wire, TLS-first bytes, no PTY, bounded stderr), rotation/enrollment lifecycle, copied-key halves, revocation fencing, stale-read integrity, recovery bypasses, concurrency/stall races, role swap, and the v4 loader gate. Test-only leaf; no production file changed. P3 notes closed (`ax-host/2` vector, bad-destination deadline hook).\\n- F1: when the SERVER refuses mid-handshake, production `Dial` stably reports `transport_failure` (alert/close rendezvous; TLS 1.3 lets the client finish first) while `Serve` deterministically reports `authentication_failed`; only the initiator's OWN verification failure surfaces as `authentication_failed` on `Dial`. Tests pin both sides; the rendezvous resolves at the hello bound.\\n- F2 (MEASURED BOUND): an idle stream with zero traffic does NOT self-close within one second of revocation — `serveLoop` carries no background watchdog. The next dispatch fences in milliseconds and `WatchGeneration` reports the commit; recorded as a stated bound with log evidence, not a pass. Tailscale SSH and non-host lanes likewise bounded.\\n- F3: `os/exec.Cmd.Wait` called twice hangs the second caller forever — test cleanup consumes one `Wait` channel. The 8 MiB line cap is enforced twice (framing + decode), so the oversize mutant weakens both layers in one multi-file probe (harness extended for `(file, old, new)` triples). The Structured Error schema URN is `urn:ax:schema:error`; a drift vector with the wrong URN passed for the wrong reason until the mutant survived and exposed it.\\n- MUTATION EVIDENCE: 9 new narrowing probes, all killed by named `TestHostile*` vectors (same-family ALPN, dual-layer oversize, client rebind, rpc-contracts, error-version drift, truncated-dispatch ignore, snapshot integrity, correlation, static nonce); pre-existing 26 probes re-run green (neutral passed, client-cache documented SURVIVED). Per-plant logs/tables in the outcome tar.\\n- TRACEABILITY: `AC-HOST-001` registered over 20 suite tests; new `unevidenced` bindings for 11.10.1–11.10.4 + 16.1 with honest gaps (executed lanes vs stated bounds); 6.6/11.10 gaps refreshed; 11.10.5 stays unowned by design (no policy reader); digest re-pinned `e327bb08...`; report 102 cases / 61 bindings / 8 unowned / 17/487 clauses; README figures + tracecheck pins updated.\\n- AC: 7 of 7 hostile rows + 13 of 13 executed AC-HOST-001 rows driven through production entries by named tests (matrix in the outcome evidence). Candidate UNCOMMITTED in the Story worktree; no review acceptance or main integration claimed. NOTE: `task-board worktree refresh-candidate` replay against `origin/main e4e3e88` fails on a LOGBOOK.md rebase conflict (missing replay resolution) — orchestrator-side integration issue, worktree untouched at `244a7dc`.\\n\\n## 2026-09-17\\n\\n### TASK-260917-3lt2xv — release-agnostic cataloggen check via -adopted\\n- CONTRACT: validation command 21 was pinned to explicit v0.6.0 inputs, so a Story re-pointing the catalog at a new revision failed construction at its own gate. The fix declares the adopted release once (`catalog.Adopted`, consumed by `Current()`) and adds a cataloggen `-adopted` mode deriving `internal/catalog/catalog.<adopted>.json` and `internal/specpin/<adopted>.lock.json` relative to `-root` (default \\\".\\\"). Mixed `-adopted` with explicit `-metadata`/`-contracts`, a missing derived input (message names the derived path), and a lock whose source release differs from adopted are refused before generation; otherwise the same Generate call and `-check`/`-output` semantics run byte-identically to the explicit form.\\n- GATE: command 21 is now `go run ./internal/catalog/cmd/cataloggen -adopted -output internal/catalog/catalog_gen.go -check`; every other validation command unchanged. No catalog content, metadata, lock, or generated-output change.\\n- TESTS: adopted positives, byte-identity (adopted vs explicit v0.6.0 vs committed), and all refusals driven through the production `run` entry; the configured-command test asserts the `-adopted` shape and runs it rooted at the repo. Narrowing mutants per refusal plus a byte-identity derivation mutant, all killed; harmless control SURVIVED. Both the candidate `-adopted` command and trunk's explicit command are green on the tree.\\n- DOCS: README regenerate block and tool row document the `-adopted` form and the explicit equivalent. No behavior or availability claims added.\\n\\n### TASK-260830-z1yxg9 — RPC envelope/hello + Host Channel 1.0.0 implemented\\n\",\n  \"original_output_bytes\": 5585,\n  \"original_output_tokens\": 1397,\n  \"truncated\": false\n}","final_result":true}}}
