{"schema_version":1,"id":"018f0000-0000-7000-8000-00000000d115","stream":{"kind":"session","id":"01a0aece-231f-7991-85b6-ba6bca7c9720"},"sequence":1765,"recorded_at":1780531400003525,"record_type":"event","durability":"durable","causation_id":"e70d9852-000b-4121-b33e-b53bebd87eae","payload_type":"task.lifecycle.output","payload_schema_version":1,"payload":{"kind":"task_lifecycle","command_id":"e70d9852-000b-4121-b33e-b53bebd87eae","run_stream":{"kind":"run","id":"e70d9852-000b-4121-b33e-b53bebd87eae"},"task_stream":{"kind":"task","id":"01a0aee5-21ad-75c1-9395-6427fbb688de"},"task_id":"01a0aee5-21ad-75c1-9395-6427fbb688de","event":{"kind":"output","task_id":"01a0aee5-21ad-75c1-9395-6427fbb688de","chunk":"Read text file `/Users/iv/Developer/ReluxWorks/agent-session-manager/.temp/STORY-260830-1kiyj6/worktree/internal/hostchannel/README.md`.\n1|# Host Channel (`internal/hostchannel`)\n2|\n3|Mutual TLS 1.3 host authentication plus the authorized RPC-5 hello:\n4|Section 11.10 Host Channel 1.0.0 over Mesh RPC 5.0.0. This package is the\n5|authenticated runtime consumer of `internal/rpcwire`.\n6|\n7|Authority: relux-works/agent-session-manager-spec@v0.6.0\n8|(commit `0cbdf100dbf84df50c64f792b1f940e3a67859a6`), sections 11.1\n9|(bilateral host admission), 11.2-11.3, 11.9, 11.10-11.10.1, 11.10.4\n10|(HC-* gates) and 17 (structured errors). Section 11.10.5 is an upstream\n11|synthetic source validator, not an AX runtime JSON-policy reader, and is\n12|not implemented here.\n13|\n14|## What it does\n15|\n16|- Runs one channel over an ordered binary duplex `Stream`\n17|  (`io.Reader`/`io.Writer`/`Close`: no listener, no PTY, no SSH process).\n18|- Negotiates mutual TLS 1.3 exactly: version floor and ceiling 1.3, ALPN\n19|  `ax-host/1`, enrolled roots only (never the system pool), mandatory\n20|  verified client certificates, no session tickets, no client cache, no\n21|  resumption, no early data, no fallback.\n22|- Supplements (never replaces) standard chain/name/time/EKU verification\n23|  with the enrolled-identity checks: exact ALPN presence, no resumption,\n24|  standard-verified chain, exactly one exact enrolled leaf/root/key match,\n25|  current Host Credential Profile 1 validity, and an admitting trust\n26|  state (active, or retiring before `retire_at`).\n27|- Exchanges one hello per side with fresh nonces, the exact RPC-5\n28|  25-key contract map, and the 8 MiB line / 5 MiB object floors. Both\n29|  hello IDs are checked: the *received* ID must equal the verified\n30|  enrolled UUID of the presenting peer under the *current* authorization\n31|  generation, and the client TLS server name must equal the selected\n32|  configured destination. The hello success is validated before any\n33|  other operation moves.\n34|- Dispatches authorized post-hello calls (`Handler`) and guards every\n35|  mutation boundary (`WithMutationAuthorization`) under the current\n36|  generation. A trust commit invalidates bound streams: dispatch,\n37|  sending, and mutation recheck currency and refuse stale bindings.\n38|- Frames refusals exactly once per the contract, then closes: identity\n39|  `host_identity_mismatch`, allowlist `peer_not_allowlisted` (both exit\n40|  7), contract `incompatible_protocol` (exit 6, only when actually\n41|  known). Unframeable input and foreign RPC majors close without a\n42|  frame. Before TLS completes, only standard TLS alerts move, never\n43|  JSON. Initiator-local failures map to `authentication_failed` (7),\n44|  `transport_failure` (8), and `invalid_config` (3).\n45|\n46|## What it does not do\n47|\n48|- No `ax` command, no SSH process launch, no listener: `LaunchArgv` and\n49|  `LaunchForConfig` only *compute* the specified remote argv\n50|  (`ax rpc serve --stdio --host-channel 1.0.0`) under Configuration 4.\n51|  Real process/SSH wiring and CLI exit mapping are later leaves.\n52|- No operation semantics: bodies stay opaque; unknown operations and\n53|  handler errors frame `incompatible_protocol`. Merkle verification,\n54|  object exchange, negotiation, and schema membership belong elsewhere.\n55|- No durable state: a channel run performs no file writes (static and\n56|  runtime censuses prove it). Trust commits are the caller's.\n57|- No clock skew, no retries, no fallback majors on the channel.\n58|\n59|## Entries\n60|\n61|- `Serve(stream, config)` runs the responder core; `Dial(stream,\n62|  config)` opens the initiator side; `(*Client).Call(op, body)` sends\n63|  one authorized post-hello request; `WatchGeneration` reports a commit\n64|  past the bound generation.\n65|- `ClientTLS`/`ServerTLS` build the profile; `VerifyPeer` is the\n66|  supplement; `EnrollmentPool` builds roots plus the CA-list bound;\n67|  `RunHandshake` enforces the deadline and byte cap by closing the\n68|  stream; `NewRequestID` mints UUIDv7 correlators; `ServerName` derives\n69|  destination SANs; `LocalFailure` maps errors to initiator codes/exits.\n70|- Timeouts: 10 s handshake, 10 s hello, configured RPC timeout (default\n71|  300 s per 6.2). Zero selects the specified defaults; tests override.\n72|  Incoming handshake bytes cap at 1 MiB; the encoded CA DN list must fit\n73|  65,535 bytes or activation refuses.\n74|\n75|## Verification\n76|\n77|`go test ./internal/hostchannel -count=1` (race-clean): full\n78|handshake/hello/operation positives in both roles over real TLS with\n79|hosttrust-issued credentials, the ten HC-* gate families in\n80|`gates_test.go`, refusal tests that assert the exact Error 1.3.0\n81|class/exit plus close behavior, deadline/cap/generation/staleness\n82|vectors, static and runtime write censuses, and launch/config model\n83|checks. The hostile-network conformance suite (`hostile_test.go`,\n84|`hostile_carrier_test.go`, acceptance case `AC-HOST-001`) re-derives\n85|the seven story cases through `Dial`/`Serve`/`Call` with per-vector\n86|refusal classes and state censuses, and executes the real OpenSSH\n87|loopback carrier lane. `mutations.py` carries one narrowing mutant per\n88|refusal gate (see `table.md` in its output), a neutral control, one\n89|documented harmless SURVIVED control (client session cache without\n90|server tickets), and a token-preserving census-evasion mutant killed by\n91|the runtime census while the static census passes.\n92|\n93|## Original acceptance rows, re-derived through this consumer\n94|\n95|| Row | Driven through | Test |\n96|| --- | --- | --- |\n97|| Request/response correlation | `Dial` + `Call` + `Serve` | `TestFullHandshakeHelloAndOperation`, `TestHelloResponseCorrelation` |\n98|| Hello maps and nonce echo | `Dial` + `Serve` hello exchange | `TestFullHandshakeHelloAndOperation`, `TestRefusesInvalidHello/*` |\n99|| Inventory namespace/cardinality | `Call(\"inventory.roots\")` dispatch | `TestInventoryRootsThroughChannel` |\n100|| Offered limits (line/object floors) | hello validation both roles | `TestFullHandshakeHelloAndOperation`, `TestOversizeHelloLine` |\n101|| Historical Structured Error framing | refusal frames via `Serve`, mapping via `Dial` | `TestRefusesNonHelloBeforeHello`, `TestHelloFailureMapping/*` |\n102|| Bilateral admission before dispatch | `AuthorizeDispatch` at hello both roles | `TestRefusesHelloUUIDMismatch`, `TestRefusesServerHelloUUIDMismatch`, `TestRefusesNotAllowlisted`, `TestRefusesDestinationMismatch` |\n103|| Deadlines and generation recovery | bounded reads/writes, stale gates, watch | `TestHelloDeadline/*`, `TestDispatchTimeout`, `TestStaleGenerationAtDispatch/*`, `TestStaleGenerationAtMutation`, `TestWatchGeneration` |\n104|\n105|Stated bounds instead of tests: native Tailscale SSH and non-host\n106|platform lanes (no SSH-implementation branch exists; the same profile\n107|runs over any `Stream`, and the OpenSSH lane is executed by\n108|`TestHostileRealCarrierOpenSSH`), the one-second self-close of an idle\n109|stream with zero traffic (measured: the next dispatch fences and\n110|`WatchGeneration` reports the commit; `serveLoop` carries no background\n111|watchdog — see `TestHostileRevocationLivePeer/idle_observation`), and\n112|TLS alert text (owned by crypto/tls). Post-hello re-hello is plain\n113|dispatch, pinned by `TestRehelloIsPlainDispatch` and\n114|`TestHostileReplay/rehello_is_inert_redispatch`.","final_result":true}}}
